.TH "CSSUNPARSEDVALUE.FOREACH" "3JS" "August 15, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSUnparsedValue.forEach \- CSSUnparsedValue: forEach() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]forEach()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]CSSUnparsedValue\f[R] interface executes a provided function once
for each item in the object.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
forEach(callbackFn)
forEach(callbackFn, thisArg)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]callbackFn\f[R]
The function to execute for each element, taking three arguments:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]currentValue\f[R]
The item being processed.
.TP
\f[B]index\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
The index of the current element being processed.
.TP
\f[B]array\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
The \f[CR]CSSUnparsedValue\f[R] that \f[CR]forEach()\f[R] is being
called on.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]thisArg\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
Value to use as \f[CR]this\f[R] when executing \f[CR]callbackFn\f[R].
.SS Return value
None (\f[CR]undefined\f[R]).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Iterating with forEach()
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] value = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSUnparsedValue([\(dq1em\(dq, \(dq#445566\(dq, \(dq\-45px\(dq]);

value.forEach((fragment, index) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(index, fragment);
});
\f[I]// 0 \(dq1em\(dq\f[R]
\f[I]// 1 \(dq#445566\(dq\f[R]
\f[I]// 2 \(dq\-45px\(dq\f[R]
.EE
